{{Story head|In 1090, after making meticulous preparations, [[Kal'tsit]] and [[Theresa]] finally awaken the [[Doctor]], who for the first time makes direct contact with the civilizations of [[Terra]].}}
{{sc|black|mode=background}}
{{sc|Priestess|I prepared a gift for you, {nickname}.<br/>What do you hear?}}
{{sc|???|This is...}}
{{sc|Priestess|Do you remember? This is the polarization formed when [[Kal'tsit|AMa-10]] was born. You said you found a rhythm within its waveform. Of course, I added a little personal touch.<br/>I adjusted the direction of the planetary track's array to capture different echoes. The harmony is derived from the lingering neutrinos of extinguishing stars. As for the orchestrator, I used the gravitational folds left behind when the ship sailed through the stargate.<br/>Oh... I knew you'd like it, {nickname}.}}
{{sc|???|The universe's singing... Even at this moment, it's still as touching as ever.<br/>But this violates the norms we set ourselves, [[Priestess]]. These facilities should've kept operating on the preset path.}}
{{sc|Priestess|The stars are losing their color. This world no longer has norms, doesn't it?<br/>This place will fall silent soon, almost like we've never been here.}}
{{sc|???|......}}
{{sc|Priestess|Come walk with me, before the silence comes.<br/>I hope... we'll get to see this world's future with our own eyes together, {nickname}.}}
{{sc|glitches|mode=background}}
{{sc|"We will... I will wait for you in that world."|mode=speech}}
{{sc|1|mode=background}}
{{sc|Four Years Ago...<br/>Summer, 1090|mode=subtitle}}
{{sc|[[Rhodes Island]] of [[Babel]], [[Kazdel]]|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Closure|Phew! Finally done retrofitting the electrical wiring. Now we're gonna be able to withstand any impact... I think.<br/>How dare Kal'tsit make me work forty-eight hours nonstop... Once all this is over, I'm gonna tell Her Highness on her!}}
{{sc|[[Scout]] replies via his communicator.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Scout|Confirmed within the landship's communications range. Signal's clear. The mini bases you hid around are great, [[Closure]].}}
{{sc|Closure|Of course! Not even [[Theresa|Her Highness]] has seen anything this handy!}}
{{sc|Scout|Is their so-called research finished?}}
{{sc|Closure|The energy surge caused by the last couple rounds almost got Rhodes Island to stall. I'm still reinforcing the landship for the next impact.<br/>You know how much I racked my brains to cover up the landship's movement? Like, what if the [[Military Commission of Kazdel|Military Commission]]'s spies caught wind—}}
{{sc|Ascalon joins the call.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Ascalon|Relax. I've already eliminated all our targets nearby. Just focus on your preparations.<br/>Scout, report.}}
{{sc|Scout|The infiltration mission is complete. I'm sending the intel back to Babel.}}
{{sc|Ascalon|What's the situation inside the city?}}
{{sc|Scout|Not much has changed over the past few years. Not many Catastrophes. Very little movement.<br/>Our situation's not very optimistic, actually. If the Military Commission continues to shrink our strategic space—}}
{{sc|Ascalon|Let's trust Her Highness and Dr. [[Kal'tsit]].}}
{{sc|Scout|You're right... They've spent so much time preparing for today's experiment just to turn the tide.}}
{{sc|Closure|Right, Scout, have you gotten your hands on the equipment I was keeping at my place?}}
{{sc|Scout|I've already entrusted it to a Messenger to take to Babel.}}
{{sc|Closure|Awesome. With the secret weapon Kal'tsit and I knocked out together, we'll definitely crack that weird control system on the ship.}}
{{sc|Ascalon|I'll rendezvous with the [[Catastrophe Messenger|Messenger]] and confirm the package's risk level before bringing it to the landship.<br/>We have been investigating the agent behind our missing engineer too. The threat against the landship hasn't been fully eliminated yet.}}
{{sc|fades out and in|mode=background}}
{{sc|Odda|Closure, I brought you even more materials, just as you asked. They're so heavy!}}
{{sc|Closure|Thanks, [[Odda]]! Hm... Looks like now I can make more safety equipment for Her Highness and Kal'tsit.<br/>And I should install an extra line for backup. Hope there won't be any unexpected surprises this time...}}
{{sc|Odda|Do you need any help, Closure?}}
{{sc|Closure|Oh. You should hurry and evacuate to a safe zone with everybody else. The next wave of impacts... is probably gonna be in thirty minutes.}}
{{sc|Odda leaves.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Closure|Now everything's all ready.<br/>Hm... I'm kinda curious... Just what kind of secret experiments are Kal'tsit and Her Highness running? They even need to mod the energy and defense modules, not to mention those weird tests...}}
{{sc|2|mode=background}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|There is no one with a better understanding of [[Originium]].}}
{{sc|Theresa|......}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|If you want to solve the suffering caused by Originium...<br/>There is no better candidate for the job.}}
{{sc|Theresa|The news you bring is always so... surprising. Even for the [[Kazdel/Overview#King of Sarkaz|King of Sarkaz]]...<br/>Are those devices really still working...? Are you confident about the resurrection?<br/>The vast majority of lifeforms on [[Terra]] can't resist corrosion that spans such a long stretch of time.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|......<br/>The Terra we see today is no doubt a miracle, and so are you, Theresa.<br/>But in the past, the whole solar system revolving around the sun was insignificant in their eyes.}}
{{sc|Theresa|You seem a little tense... and also a little anxious and nervous.<br/>Is there anything else that worries you?}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|...Yes.<br/>But... I can't tell you.}}
{{sc|Theresa|It's okay! Sorry, I shouldn't have distracted you. Focus. I can feel it.<br/>......<br/>"Kal'tsit..." You love this name, don't you?}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|......<br/>I... I've forgotten almost everything else about those days.<br/>But I still remember how, in that distant, distant past, somebody gave me this name—<br/>"Kal'tsit."<br/>That was the last time we ever met.}}
{{sc|fades out|mode=background}}
{{sc|"Kal'tsit. I do not have much time left.<br/>"Search for traces of life. Search for hope and a future.<br/>"Kal'tsit... Go find your own answer.<br/>"Find yourself."|mode=speech}}
{{sc|49 i06 1|mode=image}}
{{sc|Theresa|Then why hesitate?}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|I know what you mean. It's just...<br/>...I've had a premonition... worry... or perhaps, a conjecture.<br/>At the starting point of this land, at a certain point in time when life had only started budding, something that can never be reversed happened here.<br/>And I don't know what it is.}}
{{sc|Theresa|If it's someone that even Dr. Kal'tsit can put her full faith in, then I'm not one bit worried.<br/>Besides, considering how cautious you are, the safety measures that you prepared well ahead of time have never allowed me to worry.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|I'm sorry to say this, Theresa.<br/>This alone, no matter how many contingency measures I prepare, I still can't confidently say anything is conclusive.<br/>Theresa, I can't guarantee that I will always make the most rational decision.<br/>And this time... I want to believe.}}
{{sc|Theresa|Then do what you want to. I'll be here, with you.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit's hand touches the door that has stood silently still for a cryptically long stretch of time.<br/>A new wave of tremors reaches Rhodes Island.<br/>The door loosens.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|"Originium will become the beacon, condensed by our civilization...<br/>"If one day, other lifeforms in the universe lose their homeland and seek a way to resolve their plight,<br/>"they will witness...<br/>"...that we once shined,<br/>'we once resisted,<br/>'and this is where we rest.<br/>"We once delivered a gift to those who came after us, before our annihilation—<br/>"—Hope."|mode=subtitle}}
{{sc|The door creaks open...|mode=action}}
{{sc|49 i06 2|mode=image}}
{{sc|???|(Unknown language) This place...<br/>(Unknown language) Is... it... time already?}}
{{sc|Warning: Unknown power activated.<br/>Warning: [[PRTS]] access detected...<br/>Warning: PRTS access detect—<br/>PRTS access reset complete. Administrator permissions confirmed.<br/>All communication module channels open. Communications receiver module overclocking procedure completed.<br/>Search: [[Preserver]]... No signal.<br/>Search: [[Caerula Arbor]]... No signal.<br/>Search: [[Celestial Fulcrum]]... No signal.<br/>Search: (Unknown static noise)... No signal.<br/>......<br/>Search complete. No signal detected on any channel.<br/>Would you like to retry—|mode=speech}}
{{sc|???|(Unknown language) No... answer...<br/>(Unknown language) Just... me...<br/>(Unknown language) How long... has it been?}}
{{sc|Searching progress logs...<br/>Latest update: Four million, seven hundred fifty-five thousand, nine hundred and fifty-four days ago.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|???|......}}
{{sc|Abnormal vital signs detected. Loading restoration module.<br/>Restoring—|mode=speech}}
{{sc|???|(Unknown language) Did I... wake up too early... or... too late?<br/>(Unknown language) What stage... has Originium reached?}}
{{sc|Searching Originium inspection history data... No response.<br/>Originium inspection module is disconnected.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|???|......<br/>(Unknown language) "Terra..."<br/>(Unknown language) Why save... all these... redundant information...<br/>(Unknown language) This... isn't recorded in the database... A new language?<br/>(Unknown language) A new civilization... is born...?<br/>(Unknown language) It's... just... me... What about her...? Priestess? My...}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|(Unknown language) I can answer your question. I saved those data in PRTS in advance.}}
{{sc|???|(Unknown language) You...?}}
{{sc|A hint of unfamiliarity, perplexity, and... vigilance flashed in the eyes of the person stuck in the past.<br/>Kal'tsit senses it from the glare of the person in the sarcophagus.<br/>Likewise, Theresa senses Kal'tsit's nervousness.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|???|(Unknown language) Wait...<br/>......<br/>......<br/>(Unknown language) You've changed a fair bit...}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|......}}
{{sc|The person inside the sarcophagus feels like they have just woken up from a short dream.<br/>The lifeform that bid them farewell prior to sleep is still here by their side.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|???|(Unknown language) ...but you've never left.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|(Unknown language) No... From the moment I left this place until now, when I am standing here before you again—<br/>(Unknown language) I have wandered for thousands of years.<br/>(Unknown language) However, I have never forgotten the question you left me—}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit waits uneasily. She needs to make sure...<br/>She needs to make sure that her hope has not gone through some kind of horrible change.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|???|......<br/>(Unknown language) That... was not... a question. That was... what I looked forward to...<br/>(Unknown language) Then... Have you found the meaning of your life yet?}}
{{sc|"Kal'tsit..."|mode=subtitle}}
{{sc|2|mode=background}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|(Unknown language) Discovering the meaning in the continuation of life... It's a path that I will have to keep walking.<br/>(Unknown language) You still remember...}}
{{sc|???|(Unknown language) I still remember... To me, it was like yesterday when we said goodbye to each other, but it also seemed like an eternity...<br/>(Unknown language) But to you...}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|(Unknown language) There was never a moment when I forgot all you have done for me.<br/>(Unknown language) Aside from my life, you granted me one other thing that I found most precious—Freedom, Dr. {nickname}.}}
{{sc|???|(Unknown language) Please... just [[Doctor]] will do, Kal'tsit.}}
{{sc|Doctor|(Unknown language) Let me... get out first...}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|(Unknown language) You are still very weak. I can help—}}
{{sc|Doctor|(Unknown language) No need...<br/>(Unknown language) Kal'tsit, I still... have many questions.<br/>(Unknown language) What has become of Originium...? I couldn't find any records.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|......<br/>(Unknown language) It still grows on the continent outside.}}
{{sc|Doctor|(Unknown language) So I woke up too early.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|......}}
{{sc|Doctor|(Unknown language) You've suffered, Kal'tsit.<br/>(Unknown language) I can tell from your eyes. You woke me up because you need my help?}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|(Unknown language) Yes, ''we'' need your help.}}
{{sc|Doctor|(Unknown language) I see. That "devil"?<br/>(Unknown language) I can see from your friend behind you that not only has Originium found an unexpected way to exist...<br/>(Unknown language) She also possesses... yes, ''[[Civilight Eterna]].''}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|(Unknown language) The course of this civilization is... very complicated.}}
{{sc|Doctor|(Unknown language) What's her name...? Does their civilization have anything like that used to refer to individuals?}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|Theresa.}}
{{sc|Doctor|The... re... sa...}}
{{sc|The awakened one walks up to Theresa and holds out two arms, showing the palms of those hands.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|49 i21 1|mode=image}}
{{sc|Theresa extends her hands to lightly hold the hands of the one from the past.<br/>The Doctor feels warmth.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Theresa|Yes, Theresa.}}
{{sc|This is the moment two civilizations make contact with one another, yet Theresa can see sadness in the eyes of this Doctor from eras long gone.<br/>And she feels no warmth from the hands she is holding.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Doctor|Originium... and you... together.}}
{{sc|Theresa|You speak our language?}}
{{sc|Doctor|I... learned... from... records. Not... hard.}}
{{sc|Theresa|Unbelievable! I was thinking about learning your language. Kal'tsit said—}}
{{sc|Doctor|My world... is lost. Languages of the past... should stay in the past.<br/>I... am curious about your kind. You found... and even entered... ''Civilight Eterna.''<br/>I... want to... ask—<br/>Ask you everything about your... civilization.<br/>That's the only way... I can find traces of my world... the world of the past.}}
{{sc|Theresa|...I understand.<br/>Hm, ''Doctor'', Is that how you say it? Please forgive me. Keep holding my hands.<br/>I will show you—}}
{{sc|The Doctor cannot help but be attracted to the eyes of this creature that looks like a devil.<br/>Through her eyes, the one who lost a world sees—<br/>Life.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|3|mode=background}}
{{sc|Theresa|Civilization is born from the instinct of living beings. It's survival of the fittest.<br/>Natural selection. This is how the cycle of life is formed.}}
{{sc|Burdenbeast|(Feeble wailing)}}
{{sc|A burdenbeast accidentally fell beneath the ice pushes a small cub up from the water with its head.<br/>The small burdenbeast staggers on the ice and walks toward the hunters who are waiting afar with their bait.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Kjerag Hunter|It's coming this way. Get ready.}}
{{sc|The hunter grabs the starving burdenbeast cub before the ice cracks underneath them.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Kjerag Hunter|Good. At least we managed to save one.}}
{{sc|Theresa|Rebellion. Going against our survival instinct is the catalyst of our civilization's evolution.}}
{{sc|4|mode=background}}
{{sc|Theresa|And curiosity... curiosity is what we burn our lives away for, the staircase that allow our civilization to proceed forward.}}
{{sc|A pioneer chasing the stars is pushing forward with his fallen ally on his back.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Weary Pioneer|*pant*... *pant*... You dipshit... Why can't you keep at it for just one more day?!<br/>The newspapers already said that it was the crashed aircraft of the Wrights, not a shooting star! But you just had to get to the bottom of it!<br/>They were failures who crashed from the sky! What was there to risk your life for?<br/>Those rocks that fell onto the land? What did you want to prove to me?}}
{{sc|black|mode=background}}
{{sc|Theresa|I, too, once saw within the Black Crown the sun getting engulfed, with darkness shrouding the whole continent.<br/>But even in its darkest hour, there were still those who tried to light up the night.}}
{{sc|Curious Archosauria|It's still black! The sun really is dead!}}
{{sc|Courageous Archosauria|*sigh*... The sun's been dead for too long... We gotta save it! If the sun doesn't live, how are we going to hold our tail thickness contests?}}
{{sc|Curious Archosauria|But how?}}
{{sc|Courageous Archosauria|We climb the tallest mountain, and raise a torch up high to light it back up.}}
{{sc|Curious Archosauria|What if our arms get tired?}}
{{sc|Courageous Archosauria|Hm... then we'll build a statue of me, and my statue will hold the torch up instead.}}
{{sc|Curious Archosauria|Good idea! We can build my statue next to yours to hold up another torch, too! Then, if your torch goes out, my torch can light yours!}}
{{sc|5|mode=background}}
{{sc|Theresa|With fire comes light, and it is light that guides us toward hope.<br/>And my kin see death as a different interpretation of hope.<br/>After your body's destruction, to become one with the city within the Soul Furnace's flames is an honor bestowed only on those who are most respected.<br/>They will grow as Originium crystals and become one with Kazdel.<br/>The newborn will grow among the fluttering dust, and continue their march forward with hardships in tow amid the chorus of the myriad souls.}}
{{sc|Doctor|Progress mixed with ignorance... The cycle continues and repeats over and over.<br/>So... beautiful.<br/>So... nostalgic.<br/>Your kind... Terra seems to have gotten back on the right track... and achieving enlightenment.}}
{{sc|Theresa|How is "ignorance" defined, and how do we prove the progress of "enlightenment?"<br/>The way I see it, all of this is part of our civilization.}}
{{sc|Doctor|But the things you showed me... Most of them are... extremely different compared to your race.}}
{{sc|Theresa|Conquerors and the conquered, both have been branded with inerasable marks by this land throughout the evolution of civilization...<br/>For the sake of survival, I believe that all discrepancies will be unified, and all clans will become one.<br/>In the future that I envision, all the many lands will become one.}}
{{sc|Doctor|That's a stirring belief... It's admirable.<br/>I can feel that... you truly love this great land.<br/>Be it discrimination, war, or disaster... The object of your love has long surpassed an individual or a clan.<br/>But if you... surpass the extremes of the civilization you belong to... no one will be able to comprehend your love.<br/>On the contrary... they will loathe you.}}
{{sc|Theresa|......}}
{{sc|Doctor|Do you understand what you will have to go through... to reach the future you strive for?}}
{{sc|Theresa|If there is no choice but to walk that path, I will gladly do so.}}
{{sc|Doctor|Theresa. A Terran.<br/>No wonder Kal'tsit trusts you. She willingly took the risk to wake me in order to help you.<br/>Right. When every era comes to an end, there are always those who try their hardest to change the tide in the final moments.<br/>But most of the time, their stories don't end well.}}
{{sc|Theresa|......}}
{{sc|Doctor|Nevertheless, there is no doubt that you have my admiration.<br/>After all, on a certain level, you are very similar to some people that I knew.<br/>I will never get to see them again...<br/>......<br/>...Perhaps I'll need some more time to get my thoughts in order.<br/>But no matter. I think I should... listen to what you two have to say first.<br/>What do you need me to do?}}
{{sc|2|mode=background}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|Doctor, you need rest.}}
{{sc|Doctor|I'm fine.<br/>Kal'tsit. She's given me lots of surprises, but on top of that, she's given me even more challenges.<br/>Sorry... I mean "confusion".<br/>I still don't have a very good grasp of the Sarkaz language.<br/>I saw a lot of unexpected things in her. Surely you did too.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|I made enemies with her, came to know her, began to understand her wish, and finally admired her responsibility...<br/>That Black Crown shared with Theresa the long history and experience it bears, and she too slowly gained foresight that no other can attain.<br/>I felt... perhaps this would be our best chance. With her, with Babel, and with Terra.}}
{{sc|Doctor|"With Terra."<br/>You, too, are part of 'this great land' now, Kal'tsit.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|I hope you will take this journey with us, too.}}
{{sc|Doctor|Right...<br/>I envy you, and I trust you, Kal'tsit.<br/>But I am just a researcher. Perhaps the help I can offer won't be as significant as you hoped.}}
{{sc|Theresa|Oripathy, [[Catastrophe]]... Disasters that we have no methods to resist have been bringing many hardships to these lands... yet Terra's technology is almost entirely built atop the foundation that is Originium.<br/>Fighting over energy, the discrimination against the Infected, and the estrangement between war and races are all further tearing these lands apart...<br/>We tried, but our efforts yielded very little... That's because we know practically nothing about Originium. We know nothing about this great land.<br/>What happened to the sky and the ocean? Where did the ancient ruins come from? How exactly... were we born?<br/>We hope you'll be able to find answers for us.}}
{{sc|Doctor|Surely, Kal'tsit must already have shared some of those with you.<br/>As for Originium, I'm sorry to say that the person I am now can't give you a good answer. At the very least, not an answer to everything.<br/>When I woke up, I tried to access the logs tracking Originium's progress, but strangely, there was nothing.<br/>And this glimpse of Terra that you showed me has made me even more confused.<br/>The development of Originium... has taken a completely different turn from what I expected. I need some time.<br/>I need to explore and see this great land for myself, to understand how exactly Originium has influenced culture, life, and environment.<br/>This could take years, perhaps longer... And maybe, after an enormous amount of energy is expended, you will receive only a most disappointing answer.<br/>I once made a promise to somebody. Thinking about it now, perhaps all I ever left myself or her... was regret.<br/>That's why I won't make a promise lightly, Kal'tsit. Forgive me...}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|In that case, we will wait.<br/>No matter what your answer will be, Babel will last until the day of your return, Doctor.}}
{{sc|Doctor|...Thank you.<br/>Well... sorry... but I'm a little hungry.<br/>PRTS showed me that the landship has a temporary cafeteria...}}
{{sc|Theresa|That it does, but it might be a little messy there. How about I take you—}}
{{sc|Doctor|Thank you, Theresa, but no.<br/>This place has a special meaning to me, too. Let me walk there, slowly, by myself...}}
{{sc|Theresa|Okay... Be careful, Doctor.}}
{{sc|The Doctor leaves the room.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Theresa|......}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|The awakening has given the Doctor a lot of pressure, but it would seem this one is quick to adapt, and much quicker than I expected.<br/>The Doctor wants to learn all there is to learn about Terra.}}
{{sc|Theresa|A quick learner too, it seems.<br/>If the children were like the Doctor, perhaps they would have the chance to master even more languages and travel to so many places across Terra.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|Theresa, you should go back and look for the others. There should be plenty of Babel affairs that need the Chairman herself to...}}
{{sc|Theresa|......}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|Theresa?}}
{{sc|Theresa|Kal'tsit... there's something bothering me. Maybe I'm overthinking it, but I want to tell you.<br/>The Doctor seems to be very surprised by the look of Terra as it is today.}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|......}}
{{sc|Theresa|You once told me that nobody has a better understanding of Originium than the Doctor. The same Doctor who said that the development of Originium... took a completely different turn from the expected.<br/>Then what should Originium have been like? What should these lands have been like?<br/>...What should the Sarkaz have been like?}}
{{sc|1|mode=background}}
{{sc|Theresa|Is the Doctor ready to depart?}}
{{sc|Ascalon|Right. The Doctor applied for a transport, some defensive weapons, and nothing else.<br/>The Doctor stated an intent to avoid combat zones.}}
{{sc|Theresa|Alright. We'll just abide the Doctor's wishes.}}
{{sc|Ascalon|Your Highness, I would like to follow this Doctor of ours. Considering the background involved... I am worried.}}
{{sc|Theresa|Ascalon... have you ever left Kazdel?}}
{{sc|Ascalon|Left? If we count how I once chased a quarry and left the area when I was small, then I most certainly have.}}
{{sc|Theresa|That doesn't count.<br/>Go, follow and protect the Doctor, but do not interfere.}}
{{sc|Ascalon|I will keep a close eye—}}
{{sc|Theresa|No, Ascalon, calm down. I don't want you to keep an eye on anyone.<br/>I want you to go out there and see how the people in other lands live. This is a great opportunity.}}
{{sc|Ascalon|How they live?}}
{{sc|Theresa|Outside our homeland, neither war nor suffering is part of people's daily lives. Food, fashion, arts, culture... We could have so much.}}
{{sc|Ascalon|......}}
{{sc|Theresa|Many of us know this fact, but even more of us choose to ignore this fact, because most of the time we don't have the freedom to choose.}}
{{sc|Ascalon|......}}
{{sc|Theresa|Don't give me that look, Ascalon. Listen to me.<br/>At first, you followed me because you opposed Theresis's measures, but what about after this division is over?<br/>What will you do then? What will be the next stop for the countless Sarkaz who share the same idea as you?<br/>That's why you need to take a break from the war, and see the sights beyond our homeland.<br/>See the life that we should have lived.}}
{{sc|Ascalon|If that is your wish.}}
{{sc|Theresa|It is!<br/>Have a safe trip.}}
{{Table end}}

